<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">7 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 7 December, from 43 BCE to 1975.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/cicero" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cicero.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/43-bce">43 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,068 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cicero is killed on Mark Antony's orders</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Proscribed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-triumvirate">Second Triumvirate</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cicero">Marcus Tullius Cicero</a> was overtaken by soldiers near Formiae and killed. His head and hands were displayed in the Forum, where he had attacked Antony in his Philippics.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-triumvirate">Second Triumvirate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">574 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,452 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Justin II proclaims his general Tiberius caesar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During a respite from a severe mental illness, the Eastern Roman emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justin-ii">Justin II</a> proclaimed his general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> caesar and adopted him as his son. Tiberius became co-emperor in 578 and reigned until 582 as Tiberius II Constantine.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justin-ii">Justin II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1688">1688 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">338 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Apprentice boys shut the gates of Derry against a Jacobite force</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derry">Derry</a>, 13 apprentices shut the town's gates against Jacobite forces, an act of rebellion against James II. Its Protestant defenders went on to withstand a siege by James II's army for 105 days in 1689.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derry">Derry</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacobitism">Jacobitism</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1724">1724 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">302 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The mayor of Toruń and nine Lutheran officials are executed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a Protestant crowd vandalised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> college in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torun">Toruń</a> (Thorn) in Royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, the Polish supreme court blamed Mayor Johann Gottfried Rösner and nine other Lutheran officials for neglect of duty. They were sentenced to death and executed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torun">Toruń</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestantism">Protestantism</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1732">1732 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">294 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Theatre Royal, Covent Garden, opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">John Rich opened his new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> at Covent Garden with Congreve's The Way of the World. Twice rebuilt after fires, it became the Royal Opera House in 1892.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1815">1815 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">211 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marshal Ney is executed by firing squad</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michel-ney">Michel Ney</a>, whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> called 'the bravest of the brave', was shot in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> for treason after joining his former emperor during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-days-reform">Hundred Days</a>. He refused a blindfold and is said to have given the order to fire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1941">1941 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">85 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Japan attacks Pearl Harbor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Japanese carrier aircraft struck the US Pacific Fleet at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attack-on-pearl-harbor">Pearl Harbor</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a>, killing more than 2,400 Americans and sinking or damaging 19 ships. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> entered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1975">1975 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">51 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Indonesia invades East Timor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Indonesian forces invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-timor">East Timor</a> nine days after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fretilin">Fretilin</a> declared independence from Portugal. The occupation cost an estimated 100,000 to 180,000 lives before a UN-supervised vote led to independence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-timor">East Timor</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 7 December <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/columba"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/columba.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Columba</span><span class="tp">521–597</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/azzone-visconti"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/azzone-visconti.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Azzone Visconti</span><span class="tp">1302–1339</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/injo-of-joseon"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Injo of Joseon</span><span class="tp">1595–1649</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gian-lorenzo-bernini"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gian-lorenzo-bernini.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gian Lorenzo Bernini</span><span class="tp">1598–1680</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mario-soares"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Mário Soares</span><span class="tp">1924–2017</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 7 December <span class="n">9</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/cicero"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cicero.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Cicero</span><span class="tp">106–43 BCE</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/otto-ii-holy-roman-emperor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/otto-ii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Otto II, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="tp">955–983</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-iv"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-innocent-iv.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Innocent IV</span><span class="tp">c. 1195–1254</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-v-the-chaste"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/boleslaw-v-the-chaste.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bolesław V the Chaste</span><span class="tp">1226–1279</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/michel-ney"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/michel-ney.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Michel Ney</span><span class="tp">1769–1815</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-bligh"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-bligh.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William Bligh</span><span class="tp">1754–1817</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jon-sigurdsson"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jon-sigurdsson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jón Sigurðsson</span><span class="tp">1811–1879</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-de-lesseps"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-de-lesseps.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ferdinand de Lesseps</span><span class="tp">1805–1894</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/felix-houphouet-boigny"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/felix-houphouet-boigny.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Félix Houphouët-Boigny</span><span class="tp">1905–1993</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
